":[{"text":"Environmental legislation"},{"text":"Compliance"},{"text":"Inspection"},{"text":"Environmental standards"},{"text":"EIA"},{"text":"Environmental auditing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Field & Laboratory"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Water analysis"},{"text":"Air monitoring"},{"text":"Soil analysis"},{"text":"Laboratory documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Remote sensing"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"Environmental data analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Technical reporting"},{"text":"Evidence-based decision-making"},{"text":"Government documentation"},{"text":"Communication"},{"text":"Stakeholder management"}]}]},{"heading":"Ideal Graduate Profile","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong B.Sc Environmental Science graduate targeting Pollution Control Board Officer roles should aim to graduate with:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Environmental Science","strong pollution-control knowledge","environmental sampling/laboratory exposure","environmental law and compliance knowledge","EIA fundamentals","GIS","Excel/Power BI","environmental data analysis","government/research internship","competitive-exam preparation."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Best immediate targets"},{"type":"p","text":"Environmental Assistant / Scientific Assistant / Environmental Analyst / Laboratory Assistant / Field Assistant"},{"type":"p","text":"Then, depending on the applicable recruitment pathway:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Environmental/Scientific Officer","Senior Environmental Officer","Regulatory/Environmental Leadership"]},{"type":"h","text":"Most important principle"},{"type":"p","text":"Do not assume that a B.Sc Environmental Science automatically qualifies you for every Pollution Control Board Officer vacancy. Government recruitment is notification-specific, and some technical officer posts may require 